<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rome</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rome is a city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> that grew from a small settlement on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiber-river">Tiber</a> into the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>, and later the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>. As the centre of Roman power it fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, conquered the Seleucid, Ptolemaic and Macedonian kingdoms and waged long wars with the Parthian and Sasanian empires. Its imperial legacy was claimed by the Byzantine, Carolingian and Holy Roman empires, and it traded indirectly with distant powers such as Han <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksum</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rome.jpg" alt="Rome" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diliff · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trevi_Fountain,_Rome,_Italy_2_-_May_2007.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
